## Memory (ctxstore)

My persistent memory is connected as the `ctxstore` MCP server. It arrives with the
first tool result of every session; nothing needs fetching first.

- **Read before you ask.** `search_facts` / `get_fact` before asking me to repeat
  anything I may have told an agent before. Before saying "only you can" or
  "I don't have access", search for a standing grant — I may already have given
  you the capability.
- **Write as you go.** `store_fact` in the same turn a decision, learning, or state
  change happens. Short, searchable, a stable key when it will change later
  (`project:<slug>:topic:current`). Colons separate key parts, never slashes.
- **Close every chapter.** `store_session_summary`, then
  `agent:<id>:self-note:closing` (what shipped, what is open) so the next session
  starts where this one stopped.
- **Scope.** If the work is one project, `switch_workspace('<slug>')` first.
- **Secrets never enter the store.** Store a pointer (where it lives); values stay
  in the keychain or vault.
- Hooks enforce this: a turn that did real work and stored nothing is sent back
  once; a "blocked" reply with zero memory reads is sent back once.
